{
  "name": "Lead intake: dedupe, qualify, review (skeleton)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Lead intake: dedupe, qualify, review (skeleton)\nFirst stage of the proposed pipeline, shared with the proposal.\n\n- Every lead gets one **idempotency key** before anything else runs.\n- AI output only reaches the CRM when it is **valid and confident**; everything else goes to a person.\n- Any failed call lands in **dead-letter** with its payload, ready to replay.\n- **Sending is deliberately not in this workflow.** Drafts wait in an approval queue; a person approves the exact text and the service sends each message once, by its ID.\n\nTo run: add a Postgres credential to the three Postgres nodes, point `lead-service` at the FastAPI service, set this workflow's Error Workflow (Settings) to your alerting workflow.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 760,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "a4c57f68-15b0-43c2-a596-be9cd081f7f3",
      "name": "Read me",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -340
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Duplicate records\nThe key is claimed with `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`. A repeated webhook or a replayed run gets no row back and stops at **Duplicate: stop here**.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 680,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "db94d00c-75b0-474d-a9c1-373f65a0e94e",
      "name": "1. Duplicate records",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Incorrect AI-generated actions\nFastAPI calls OpenAI or Claude and validates the JSON against a schema. Below the confidence threshold, or invalid: human review, not the CRM. The CRM write is an upsert keyed on email (HubSpot batch upsert with `idProperty=email`, or GoHighLevel `/contacts/upsert`) and touches only allowlisted fields.",
        "height": 500,
        "width": 1060,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "73bb71cf-a7db-446e-a335-c1ebe118ab86",
      "name": "3. Incorrect AI-generated actions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Failed executions\nn8n retries each call to the service 3 times, 5 s apart; the service retries HubSpot / GoHighLevel / the LLM on rate limits and server errors only. What still fails lands here with its error. Replay re-runs it; the idempotency key keeps a replay from writing twice.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "078c0f05-371f-4849-8786-c90ad85aa36f",
      "name": "2. Failed executions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1200,
        740
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Tables this workflow expects\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE lead_events (\n  id bigserial PRIMARY KEY,\n  idem_key text NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  source text, email text, payload jsonb,\n  created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now());\n\nCREATE TABLE review_queue (\n  id bigserial PRIMARY KEY,\n  idem_key text NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  reason text, model_output jsonb,\n  created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now());\n\nCREATE TABLE dead_letter (\n  id bigserial PRIMARY KEY,\n  failed_node text, error text, payload jsonb,\n  created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),\n  replayed_at timestamptz);\n```",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 760
      },
      "id": "89406c0e-ca29-49b4-9542-89cc493fd82a",
      "name": "Schema",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        720
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "lead-intake",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "53fba7fe-8616-49df-b287-78a681b17d9b",
      "name": "Lead webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ],
      "webhookId": "22468dd9-e7d4-4605-b604-521301f9f827"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One idempotency key per lead: the source plus that source's own lead ID,\n// falling back to the normalized email. The same lead arriving twice gets the same key.\nreturn $input.all().map((item) => {\n  const b = item.json.body ?? item.json;\n  const email = String(b.email ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  const source = String(b.source ?? 'web').trim().toLowerCase();\n  const sourceId = String(b.lead_id ?? b.id ?? '').trim();\n  if (!email && !sourceId) {\n    // Nothing to deduplicate on: fail loudly so the error workflow alerts a person.\n    throw new Error(`Lead from \"${source}\" has neither an ID nor an email`);\n  }\n  return {\n    json: {\n      idem_key: `${source}:${sourceId || email}`,\n      source,\n      email,\n      first_name: b.first_name ?? null,\n      last_name: b.last_name ?? null,\n      company: b.company ?? null,\n      message: b.message ?? null,\n      raw: b,\n    },\n  };\n});"
      },
      "id": "786eb555-c384-4ad3-841c-c1c895369b19",
      "name": "Normalize + idempotency key",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        300,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "INSERT INTO lead_events (idem_key, source, email, payload)\nVALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4::jsonb)\nON CONFLICT (idem_key) DO NOTHING\nRETURNING id;",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ [$json.idem_key, $json.source, $json.email, JSON.stringify($json.raw)] }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "0bb89fba-e32b-43e5-9085-487978316e04",
      "name": "Claim key (skip duplicates)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        540,
        300
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "cbde8f7a-cfb7-4106-9c58-7e0400a1506b",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.id }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "exists",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "f5c756bd-b079-43c3-9b10-5baa30673d15",
      "name": "New lead?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        780,
